   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0b74b6d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Estimating pos, lin vel, ang vel and contact force\n",
    "Adding the contact force first is easier since the predict and update step can be done linearly. For that, the previous estimation of $J \\cdot \\tau$ is used as a measurement.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Kalman Filter matrices for $A$, $B$ and $H$ are:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "A = \\begin{bmatrix} \n",
    "I_3 & dt\\cdot I_3 & 0 & 0\\\\\n",
    "0 & I_3 & 0 & 0\\\\\n",
    "0 & 0 & I_3 & 0\\\\\n",
    "0 & 0 & 0 & I_{12}\\\\\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "B = \\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "0 & 0 \\\\\n",
    "dt\\cdot I_3 & 0\\\\\n",
    "0 & dt\\cdot I_3\\\\\n",
    "0 & 0\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "H = \\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "0 & dt\\cdot I_3 & 0 & 0\\\\\n",
    "0 & 0 & dt\\cdot I_3 & 0\\\\\n",
    "0 & 0 & 0 & I_{12}\\\\\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The difference between `est_mode=2` and `est_mode=3` is, for '2' the part in `A` for contact force is the identity, for '3' its the contact state diagonal block matrix.\n",
    "\n",
    "`est_mode=4` means, the base acc estimation is inside the Kalman Filter, instead of in a separate function. The Kalman Filter matrices for $A$, $B$ and $u$ are then:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "A = \\begin{bmatrix} \n",
    "I_3 & dt\\cdot I_3 & 0 & 0\\\\\n",
    "0 & I_3 & 0 & b\\\\\n",
    "0 & 0 & I_3 & \\beta\\\\\n",
    "0 & 0 & 0 & I_{12}\\\\\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "B = \\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "0 & 0 \\\\\n",
    "H_B^{-1}\\cdot (-H_{BL}) & H_B^{-1}\\cdot (-c-g)\\\\\n",
    "0 & 0\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "u = \\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "\\ddot{q}_L \\\\ 1\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "with\n",
    "$$\n",
    "b = dt \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix} \n",
    "c_1 \\cdot (H_B^{-1} \\cdot \\^{J}_1)\\\\\n",
    "c_2 \\cdot (H_B^{-1} \\cdot \\^{J}_2)\\\\\n",
    "c_3 \\cdot (H_B^{-1} \\cdot \\^{J}_3)\\\\\n",
    "c_4 \\cdot (H_B^{-1} \\cdot \\^{J}_4)\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}, \n",
    "\n",
    "\\beta = dt \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix} \n",
    "c_1 \\cdot (H_B^{-1} \\cdot \\check{J}_1)\\\\\n",
    "c_2 \\cdot (H_B^{-1} \\cdot \\check{J}_2)\\\\\n",
    "c_3 \\cdot (H_B^{-1} \\cdot \\check{J}_3)\\\\\n",
    "c_4 \\cdot (H_B^{-1} \\cdot \\check{J}_4)\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "where $J = \\begin{bmatrix} \\^{J}\\\\\\check{J} \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} I\\\\cp_x \\end{bmatrix}$"
   ]
  },
