  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a80e037",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Estimating contact state\n",
    "\n",
    "Since low cost robots often don't have contact sensors, estimating the contact state can also be useful. This approach is based on [this paper](https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/stamp/stamp.jsp?arnumber=11163249&tag=1).\n",
    "\n",
    "For that a generalized momentum disturbance observer is used:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "\\dot{\\hat{p}}\\\\\n",
    "\\dot{\\hat{f}}\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "0 & -J^T \\\\\n",
    "0 & 0\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "\\hat{p}\\\\\n",
    "\\hat{f}\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "\\bar{\\tau}\\\\\n",
    "0\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\begin{bmatrix}\n",
    "L_1 (p-\\hat{p})\\\\\n",
    "L_2 (p-\\hat{p})\n",
    "\\end{bmatrix}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "with\n",
    "\n",
    "- $p = M(x)v$ being the measured generalized momentum\n",
    "- $M$ being the joint space inertia matrix\n",
    "- $v$ the velocity\n",
    "- $\\hat{p}$ being the estimated generalized momentum\n",
    "- $\\hat{f}$ being the measured contact force\n",
    "- $J$ the contact jacobian.\n",
    "- $\\bar{\\tau} = \\tau_m + C^Tv - g$ with $\\tau_m$ being motor torque, $C$ coriolis matrix and $g$ gravity\n",
    "- $L_1, L_2$ being observer gains\n",
    "\n",
    "The force is only estimated for the z-axis and clipped to be always positive. For each foot, there is a specific threshold to determine the contact state."
   ]
  },
